## 6. Work units and their named places

A work unit gets its **own named place**, and its **state is readable at a glance** from that
name. The binding states the mechanics — what a named place is on that surface, how its
address is obtained, and how the name changes on close.

| Event | Action |
|---|---|
| Lane spawned for issue `#N` | Give the work unit its own named place, in the spawn state |
| Lane reports complete | Flip the name to the closed state, leaving it in place |
| Lane blocked | Post the block in that place and notify `HQ` |

The address is stable across the rename and is what a scheduled job's delivery points at.
**Rename, never re-create.**

> **A named place is not a lane.** On this binding the place exists as soon as it is created,
> but a session is bound to it only by a message *arriving* there. Until that happens, the
> place is addressable and unowned — anything delivered to it parks, and "the lane is up" is
> an assumption. The binding carries the mechanics and the current blocker for creating one
> without an operator's hand.

